# Insurance Premium Calculator

This is a basic insurance pricing model built in Microsoft Excel. It calculates an insurance premium based on user-input values for customer age and risk category.

## 🧮 What It Does

- Accepts customer age and a risk category (Low, Medium, High)
- Applies a base premium and adjusts it using:
  - A risk multiplier
  - An age-based factor (+1% for every year over 30)
- Outputs a final premium

## 🛠 Tech Used

- Excel formulas (VLOOKUP, IF logic)
- Conditional formatting
- Simple user inputs and calculated output

## 📌 Why This Exists

Built as a learning project during my transition into actuarial work. It simulates how property & casualty insurers might use basic rating logic to assign premiums.

